# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
#
# No redirect/proxy rule is needed here. Cloudflare Pages serves the root
# (`/index.html`) for any incoming path that does not match a static asset
# whenever the project has NO top-level `404.html` — which is the case for this
# Vite build. That built-in behavior is the supported SPA fallback and avoids the
# `/* /index.html 200` proxy rule, which Cloudflare rejects as an infinite loop
# (the `*` also matches `/index.html`, so the proxy would recurse onto itself).
# Direct navigation/refresh on `/login`, `/dashboard`, etc. is therefore handled
# client-side by the history router (`client/src/components/router.tsx`).
#
# IMPORTANT: browser API calls use relative /api/* paths. Route /api/* to the
# VPS Express backend at the edge (a Cloudflare Worker route or Cloudflare
# Tunnel) BEFORE Pages. Worker routes take precedence over Pages entirely, so
# /api/* must never be served by the static SPA fallback.
